            <ArticleTitle>[Silent myocardial ischemia and arrhythmia in patients with stage II-IV arterial occlusive disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>330-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Holter-monitoring offers a possibility to detect asymptomatic coronary-heart-disease-patients, suffering from peripher-arteric-occlusion stadium II-IV, and introduce them to effective medication. It became evident, that about 30% of all patients with unknown coronary-heart-disease, even as patients who were therapied against coronary-heart-disease, have had silent myocard ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
